🏥 Heart Failure Prediction System
This project is an MLOps-ready web application that predicts the risk of heart failure based on clinical patient data. It uses a Random Forest Classifier to analyze patterns and a StandardScaler to ensure data consistency.

🚀 Project Overview
Goal: Predict the DEATH_EVENT (High Risk vs. Low Risk) based on 12 clinical features.

Model: Random Forest with 100 estimators and balanced class weights to handle data imbalance.

Deployment: Built with Streamlit for real-time interaction.

📂 Repository Structure
app.py: The Streamlit web application code.

code.ipynb: The Jupyter Notebook containing the data analysis and training logic.

heart_disease_model.pkl: The trained Random Forest "Chef".

scaler.pkl: The StandardScaler "Translator" used for preprocessing.

requirements.txt: List of dependencies required for deployment.

🛠️ Installation & Local Usage
Clone the repository:

Bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/project01_heart_disease.git
Install dependencies:

Bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
Run the application:

Bash
streamlit run app.py
🧠 MLOps Concepts Implemented
Artifact Versioning: Saving the model and scaler as inseparable pairs to ensure production matches training.

Feature Scaling: Implementing standardization to prevent high-magnitude features like platelets from overpowering features like age.

Reproducibility: Using random_state=42 across all data splits and model training.
